    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31434" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰσμᾰτέομαι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>put in the hand to feel,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Art.</u>
				32
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσμασάμενος ἐς τὴν
			κοιλίην</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				46
			</span></i>; in full, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν χεῖρα ἔσω ἐσμάσασθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aret.
					<u>SD</u>
					2.9
				</span></i>
			.— The spelling 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσματευόμενον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Art.</u>
					38
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Mul.</u>
				1.70
			</span></i> (v.l.), is corrupt for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσματεύμενον,</span> while 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσματτευόμενον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Bacch.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Erot.
			</span></i> and 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσμάττεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					18
				</span></i>
			(I).<i><span class="en">
				453
			</span></i> are Atticizing forms.</div>
